isms we've had  ongoing deforestation in Indonesia which  scientists have told us now equal the  same in carbon emissions alone two US  auto emissions per year okay this means  that we need much tougher I would argue  government policies when it comes to  land use designation what land is going  to be for the working forests what land  will be a set aside for biodiversity  conservation my worry is that by giving  all attention to market mechanisms we  made two fundamental errors one but  giving markets too much attention too  much responsibility  they were burdened under the weight of  too many responsibilities and therefore  they couldn't achieve more modest  objectives that could have been in place  second by giving them everything to do  we took the problem definition off of  government agendas who said simply hey  markets are addressing this question  when that was a cop-out right the  question is how do we better integrate  find synergies among government policies  on the one hand and markets on the other  hand this requires a much more concerted  effort around the problems that we all  care about and do you think it's  possible to meld the two I actually do I  think it's not easy people call me an  optimist I think I'm just much more of a  concerned problem focused political  scientist and I see possibilities for  doing so it requires that the great  coalition we now have globally that's  emerging to address legality  verification because the strategic  self-interest of so many organizations  unite around this instrument it requires  the same  coalition think carefully about then  what they can do collectively to solve  subproblems that meet other instruments  and other tools and how can we therefore  work in a synergistic a way linking  theories of why support occurs two  strategies for better improving  on-the-ground performance around these  kinds of institutions okay are there any  other efforts that you think can be  undertaken to improve flora global  fo